# The sets of code points that a general category does not tell, in Unicode
# 17.0.0: white space, and what is lower case, upper case, alphabetic or
# passed over in casing without its category saying so. `classes.hero` reads
# them.
#
# The table is data, made and not typed: a one-off program asked Python 3.15.2's
# `unicodedata`, whose `unidata_version` is 17.0.0, and Go 1.27.3's `unicode`,
# whose `Version` is 17.0.0, on 2026-11-15, reduced their answers to ranges,
# held every lookup to the answers for each of the 1,114,112 code points, and
# wrote this module whole. Nothing here is edited by hand.
#
# Each entry is a range, `first << 21 | last`, both ends in it, ascending.

# The code points of Unicode's White_Space property.
constant WHITE_SPACE: [i64]
    [
        18874381
        67108896
        278921349
        335544480
        12079601280
        17179877386
        17263763497
        17278443567
        17379106911
        25769816064
    ]

# The code points that are lower case, Unicode's Lowercase property, and whose
# general category is not `Ll`.
